{"id":"U10","title":"The Power of Patience","titleZh":"耐心的力量","paras":[{"id":"U10-P1","sentences":[{"id":"U10-P1-S1","hard":false,"text":"Here's a riddle: What do traffic jams, long lines and waiting for a vacation to start all have in common?"},{"id":"U10-P1-S2","hard":false,"text":"There's one answer: They're all situations where we could use a little extra patience."}],"zh":"这里有一个谜语：交通堵塞、排长队和等待假期开始，这些有什么共同点？有一个答案：它们都是我们可能需要多一点耐心的情境。"},{"id":"U10-P2","sentences":[{"id":"U10-P2-S1","hard":false,"text":"In the Digital Age, we're used to having what we need immediately and right at our fingertips."},{"id":"U10-P2-S2","hard":false,"text":"However, research suggests that if we practiced patience, we'd be a whole lot better off."},{"id":"U10-P2-S3","hard":false,"text":"Here are several tricks."}],"zh":"在数字时代，我们习惯于立即获得所需，而且触手可及。然而，研究表明，如果我们练习耐心，我们的境况会好得多。这里有几个技巧。"},{"id":"U10-P3","sentences":[{"id":"U10-P3-S1","hard":false,"text":"Practice gratitude."},{"id":"U10-P3-S2","hard":false,"text":"Thankfulness has a lot of benefits: Research shows it makes us happier, less stressed and even more optimistic."},{"id":"U10-P3-S3","hard":false,"text":"It can also help us practice more patience."},{"id":"U10-P3-S4","hard":false,"text":"\"Showing thankfulness can foster self-control,\" said Ye Li, researcher at the University of California."}],"zh":"练习感恩。感恩有很多好处：研究表明它使我们更快乐、压力更小，甚至更乐观。它还能帮助我们练习更多的耐心。\"表达感恩可以培养自控力，\"加州大学研究员叶丽说。"},{"id":"U10-P4","sentences":[{"id":"U10-P4-S1","hard":false,"text":"Make yourself wait."},{"id":"U10-P4-S2","hard":false,"text":"Instant gratification may seem like the most \"feel good\" option at the time, but psychology research suggests waiting for things actually makes us happier in the long run."},{"id":"U10-P4-S3","hard":false,"text":"And the only way for us to get into the habit of waiting is to practice."},{"id":"U10-P4-S4","hard":false,"text":"Start with small tasks."},{"id":"U10-P4-S5","hard":false,"text":"Put off watching your favorite show until the weekend or wait 10 extra minutes before going for that cake."},{"id":"U10-P4-S6","hard":false,"text":"You'll soon find that the more patience you practice, the more you start to apply it to other, more annoying situations."}],"zh":"让自己等待。即时满足在当时可能看起来是最\"感觉良好\"的选择，但心理学研究表明，从长远来看，等待事物实际上会让我们更快乐。而我们养成等待习惯的唯一方法就是练习。从小事开始。把看最喜欢的节目推迟到周末，或者在去吃那块蛋糕之前多等十分钟。你很快就会发现，你练习的耐心越多，你就越开始把它应用到其他更令人烦恼的情境中。"},{"id":"U10-P5","sentences":[{"id":"U10-P5-S1","hard":false,"text":"Accept the uncomfortable."},{"id":"U10-P5-S2","hard":true,"text":"So many of us have the belief that being comfortable is the only state we will tolerate, and when we experience something outside of our comfort zone, we get impatient about the circumstances."},{"id":"U10-P5-S3","hard":false,"text":"You should learn to say to yourself, \"This is merely uncomfortable, not intolerable.\""},{"id":"U10-P5-S4","hard":false,"text":"You'll then gradually become more patient."}],"zh":"接受不舒服。我们中有太多人认为舒适是我们唯一能容忍的状态，而当我们经历舒适区之外的事情时，我们就会对情境变得不耐烦。你应该学会对自己说：\"这只是不舒服，不是无法忍受的。\"然后你就会逐渐变得更加有耐心。"}],"words":[{"id":"U10-W01","lemma":"riddle","surface":"riddle","pos":"n.","zh":"谜语; 谜题","sent":"U10-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"solve a riddle","zh":"解谜"}]},{"id":"U10-W02","lemma":"jam","surface":"jams","pos":"n.","zh":"堵塞; 果酱","sent":"U10-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"traffic jams","zh":"交通堵塞"}]},{"id":"U10-W03","lemma":"have in common","surface":"have in common","pos":"phr.","zh":"有共同之处","sent":"U10-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"have sth. in common","zh":"有...共同之处"}]},{"id":"U10-W04","lemma":"situation","surface":"situations","pos":"n.","zh":"情境; 情况; 形势","sent":"U10-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"in a situation","zh":"在某种情况下"},{"en":"current situation","zh":"当前形势"}]},{"id":"U10-W05","lemma":"extra","surface":"extra","pos":"adj. / adv. / n.","zh":"adj. 额外的; 附加的 adv. 特别地 n. 额外的东西","sent":"U10-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"extra patience","zh":"额外的耐心"},{"en":"extra time","zh":"额外的时间"}]},{"id":"U10-W06","lemma":"patience","surface":"patience","pos":"n.","zh":"耐心; 忍耐","sent":"U10-P1-S2","phrases":[{"en":"have patience","zh":"有耐心"},{"en":"lose patience","zh":"失去耐心"}]},{"id":"U10-W07","lemma":"used","surface":"used","pos":"adj.","zh":"习惯于","sent":"U10-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"be used to","zh":"习惯于..."}]},{"id":"U10-W08","lemma":"immediately","surface":"immediately","pos":"adv.","zh":"立即; 马上","sent":"U10-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"respond immediately","zh":"立即回应"}]},{"id":"U10-W09","lemma":"fingertip","surface":"fingertips","pos":"n.","zh":"指尖","sent":"U10-P2-S1","phrases":[{"en":"at one's fingertips","zh":"触手可及; 随时可用"}]},{"id":"U10-W10","lemma":"suggest","surface":"suggests","pos":"v.","zh":"表明; 建议; 暗示","sent":"U10-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"research suggests","zh":"研究表明"},{"en":"suggest doing sth.","zh":"建议做某事"}]},{"id":"U10-W11","lemma":"whole","surface":"whole","pos":"adj. / n.","zh":"adj. 整个的; 全部的 n. 整体","sent":"U10-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"a whole lot","zh":"大量; 许多"},{"en":"on the whole","zh":"总的来说"}]},{"id":"U10-W12","lemma":"better off","surface":"better off","pos":"phr.","zh":"境况更好; 更富裕","sent":"U10-P2-S2","phrases":[{"en":"be better off","zh":"境况更好"}]},{"id":"U10-W13","lemma":"trick","surface":"tricks","pos":"n.","zh":"技巧; 诀窍; 把戏","sent":"U10-P2-S3","phrases":[{"en":"several tricks","zh":"几个技巧"},{"en":"trick or treat","zh":"不给糖就捣蛋"}]},{"id":"U10-W14","lemma":"gratitude","surface":"gratitude","pos":"n.","zh":"感恩; 感激","sent":"U10-P3-S1","phrases":[{"en":"show gratitude","zh":"表达感恩"},{"en":"feel gratitude","zh":"心怀感激"}]},{"id":"U10-W15","lemma":"optimistic","surface":"optimistic","pos":"adj.","zh":"乐观的; 乐观主义的","sent":"U10-P3-S2","phrases":[{"en":"be optimistic about","zh":"对...乐观"}]},{"id":"U10-W16","lemma":"foster","surface":"foster","pos":"v.","zh":"培养; 促进; 养育","sent":"U10-P3-S4","phrases":[{"en":"foster self-control","zh":"培养自控力"},{"en":"foster growth","zh":"促进成长"}]},{"id":"U10-W17","lemma":"self-control","surface":"self-control","pos":"n.","zh":"自控力; 自我控制","sent":"U10-P3-S4","phrases":[{"en":"exercise self-control","zh":"